# __PROJECT_NAME__

A Go API laid out as a modular monolith: hexagonal feature modules on a shared
platform, with layer rules enforced by go-arch-lint. Generated by hexgen.

## Prerequisites

- Go 1.27 or later
- Docker and Docker Compose (Postgres, Redis, and the test containers)
- Make

## Quick Start

```bash
make setup            # dev tooling, and .env from .env.example
{{- if .Auth}}
# set JWT_SECRET in .env first: openssl rand -hex 32
{{- end}}
make docker-up        # start postgres and redis
make migrate-install  # goose CLI
make migrate-up       # apply db/migrations (includes River's job tables)
{{- if .Auth}}
make seed             # dev admin: admin@example.com / admin123456
{{- end}}
make run              # API on :8080
curl localhost:8080/health
```

River's schema is a goose migration (`db/migrations/*_river.sql`). When you
upgrade River, add a migration for the new schema versions from
`river migrate-get --version <n> --up` and `--down`.
{{- if .Auth}}

## Auth and Users

The `auth` and `user` modules provide:

- `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `POST /api/auth/refresh`
- `GET /api/users/me`, `PUT /api/users/me` (logged in)
- `GET /api/admin/users`, `GET|PUT|DELETE /api/admin/users/{id}`,
  `PUT /api/admin/users/{id}/role` (admin role)

The API refuses to boot while `JWT_SECRET` is the `.env.example` placeholder
or shorter than 32 bytes. The seeded admin's credentials are public: never run
`make seed` against a production database.
{{- end}}

## Project Structure

```text
cmd/api/            API entry point
internal/app/       composition root: builds every feature Service and wires their ports
internal/server/    HTTP server and router; every route is mounted in router.go
internal/config/    infrastructure env config
internal/platform/  infrastructure with no feature knowledge (database, cache, jobqueue, web, ...)
internal/testutil/  shared Postgres and Redis test containers
db/migrations/      goose migrations
```

## Adding a Feature Module

1. Create `internal/features/<name>/` with `service.go`, `repository.go`,
   `domain/`, and the adapters it needs under `adapter/` (`postgres/`, `http/`).
2. Build it in `internal/app/app.go` and add a field for it on `Services`.
3. Mount its routes on the {{if .Auth}}`authed` (logged in) or `admin` group{{else}}`api` group{{end}} in
   `internal/server/router.go`.
4. Add `ft-<name>`, `ft-<name>-domain` and `ft-<name>-adapter` to the
   components and deps in `.go-arch-lint.yml`, then run `make check-arch`.
5. Add its migration with `make migrate-create name=create_<name>s`.
6. Run `make mocks` to generate its mocks, then `make test`.
{{- if .Auth}}

### Starting from `user`

`internal/features/user` is the reference module. Copy it to
`internal/features/<name>/`, then strip what only exists for auth.

Keep, as the pattern for your module:

- `domain/user.go`: the struct, cut down to `ID`, your fields, `CreatedAt` and
  `UpdatedAt`.
- `service.go`: `GetByID`, `ListAdmin`, `AdminUpdate` and `Delete`, each with
  its tracing span. Add a `Create` for your fields.
- `repository.go` and `adapter/postgres/repository.go`: `GetByID`, `ListAdmin`
  (offset paging through `paging.OffsetPage`: a count query plus a page query)
  and `scanUser`. Replace `UpdateGuarded` with a plain `Update`, make `Delete`
  a plain `DELETE`, and add `Create`.
- `adapter/http/admin_handler.go`, `admin_request.go`, `admin_response.go`: the
  list, get, update and delete handlers and their consumer-side interface
  (`UserManager`).
- The tests for those methods. Regenerate mocks with `make mocks` instead of
  editing `mocks_test.go`.

Strip, because only auth needs it:

- `contract.go` (`Profile`, `Credentials`, `NewUser`: the types auth's port
  uses) and `toProfile`.
- `GetByEmail`, `Create(NewUser)`, `GetProfile`, `UpdateProfile`, `UpdateRole`,
  `UpdateGuarded`, `CountAdmins` and `IncrementTokenVersion`.
- The requester and last-admin guards in `AdminUpdate` and `Delete`, and the
  `requesterID` parameter.
- `Email`, `PasswordHash`, `Role`, `Active`, `TokenVersion`, and the
  `RoleUser`/`RoleAdmin` constants.
- Soft delete: `DeletedAt` and every `deleted_at IS NULL`, unless you want
  soft delete too.
- `adapter/http/handler.go`, `request.go` and `response.go`: the `/users/me`
  handler, which reads the caller from `request.RequireUser`.

Rename the module's own names, not every `user`: `package user`,
`features/user`, `domain.User`, `userpg`, `userhttp`, `UserManager`,
`*user.Service`, the `Users` field, the `users` table and the `test_user`
database. A blind find-and-replace also rewrites `request.RequireUser`,
`UserID`, `identity` and `middleware.RequireRole`, which belong to the
platform.

For the wiring and the migration, copy what `user` has:
`userMod := user.New(userpg.New(db))` and the `Users` field in
`internal/app/app.go`, the `userAdminHandler` block in
`internal/server/router.go`, the `ft-user` components and deps in
`.go-arch-lint.yml`, and `db/migrations/*_create_users.sql`.
{{- else}}

For a module to copy from, generate a scratch project with `--auth`: its
`internal/features/user` is a complete CRUD module with tests, and its README
lists what to keep and strip.
{{- end}}

